card.statement:
The endofunctors $\{\sT_i |i\in \tI\}$, $\{\sX^{\mu}|\mu\in \sfP\}$, and $\{\sv^m|m\in \bZ \}$,
categorify the action of the affine Hecke algebra in the basic representation $\bZ_t[\sfP]$
under the following correspondence:

\[ \hT_i \leftrightarrow \sT_i, \ \hX^{\mu} \leftrightarrow \sX^{\mu}, \ t \leftrightarrow \sv[1].
\]

More precisely, on the level of characters the action of endofunctors $\sT_i$, $\sX^{\mu}$ and $\sv[1]$ on $\bZ_{t}[\sfP]$ coincides with the action of the generators of AHA: $\hT_i$, $\hX^{\mu}$ and $t$ correspondingly. Moreover, there exists the following list of isomorphisms of triangulated endofunctors

\begin{gather}
\begin{array}{c}
{	\sT_i \circ \sT'_i \simeq \sT_i'\circ \sT_i \simeq \Id_{\fb {[\xi]}}; } \\
{ \sT'_i \simeq  \cone((\sv\circ\sD_i) \to \Id_{\fb {[\xi]}}[-1]) \simeq \cone((\sv\circ\cone(\sT_i[-1] \to \Id_{\fb {[\xi]}}))\to \Id_{\fb {[\xi]}}[-1])   }
\end{array}
\\
{  \sT_i \circ \sX^{\mu} \simeq \sX^{\mu} \circ \sT_i,} {~{\text if}~ \langle \mu,\alpha_i^{\vee} \rangle=0; }\\
{ \sT_i \circ \sX^{\mu}  \simeq \sv\sX^{\mu-\alpha_i}\circ\sT'_i[1],}{~{\text if}~ \langle \mu, \alpha_i^{\vee} \rangle=1.}
\\
\underbrace{\sT_i \circ \sT_j \circ \ldots }_{m_{{i,j}} \text{ factors}} \simeq \underbrace{\sT_j \circ \sT_i \circ \ldots }_{m_{{i,j}}\text{ factors}} \text{ here } m_{{i,j}} = ord_{W}(s_is_j)
\end{gather}

that categorify the corresponding defining Relations <<ref:eq::Hecke::alg>>, <<ref:eq::rel::braid1>>, <<ref:eq::rel::braid2>> and <<ref:eq::rel::braid0>> of the Affine Hecke algebra.
